      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m pretty strongly opposed to sending the old result as an async response to the request when the request has timed out. That seems misleading to the caller in such a case. We *do* send the cached result if the existing result is too new, but we only get here if the current cached result was sufficiently old to allow a new request in the first place, so at this point, the age of the last response is at least LAST_CELL_INFO_MAX_AGE + CELL_INFO_LIST_QUERY_TIMEOUT.\n\nPlaying with the timeout values is something we can continue to tweak, especially given that callers should be moving to an async API which means that only legacy callers will be blocked on a binder call. I can\u0027t imagine why it should take longer than 1s (or even half that time), but I think a reasonable timeout value is something on the order of 150%-200% of the max expected RIL latency, so if we expect 1s, then 2s is totally fine IMO.",
